& [Review]
  + the implementation promotes a new bounded crate and never makes the live untracked cantor_scribe crate a workspace member
  + strict serde shapes and explicit set deserializers close unknown-field and duplicate-set ambiguity
  + validation covers package dependency closure global identity source ownership UTF-8 spans role cardinality participant kinds expressions rules and complete views
  + source analysis is byte-bounded diagnostic-bounded recovery-capable and retains exact supplied byte offsets
  + three-valued evaluation keeps absent facts unknown and records every observed fact
  + component evidence hashes exactly ten owned files while independent custody hashes exactly six upstream files
  + the instance-contract test adds the bounded capability and independently proves the whole cantor_scribe candidate remains held

& [ThreatReview]
  + no ambient I/O database async transport process environment network provider CLI unsafe or external-effect surface exists in production crate sources or dependencies
  + digest tamper unknown fields duplicate sets invalid spans duplicate identities expression depth unsupported operators and partial parse recovery are exercised
  + capability recognition is structural nonauthority and cannot authorize execution installation provider contact mutation publication or update

& [Residuals]
  + parser grammar is intentionally bounded and is not a complete parser for every historical SOP notation
  + storage project loading query revision draft search LSP MCP and Tokio layers remain unpromoted
  + the implementation does not yet make SOP Eclipse a live hosted process or give Cantor self-update authority
  + review is agent-produced and not an independent human audit

& [Disposition]
  + acceptable_for_exact_owned_branch_publication_after_completion_signature_and_attribution
